B = [
('The Body Shop','Europe','1980s-90s','cosmetics','In the style of The Body Shop, earnest, earthy, ethical design in deep forest green and white. Glossy dark green panels carry a small white circular emblem and plain white sans-serif lettering in tidy sentence case. Clear and pale frosted plastic is paired with matte green and cream surfaces, simple thin white type and an apple-green accent. Natural textures such as jute, kraft paper, wicker and raw cotton keep things honest, with hand-written paper tags and rounded botanical line drawings of leaves, seeds and fruit in flat green, cream and warm orange. Layouts are modest, centred and informative, with plain recycled-looking paper and gentle matte finishes. Wholesome, sincere, natural and quietly proud.'),
('Penhaligons','Europe','19th century-present','perfume','In the style of Penhaligons, ornate, quirky Victorian gentleman-perfumer elegance. Cut-crystal and clear glass with faceted details are finished with silken ribbon, tassels and gilt trim. Surfaces are heavy cream, deep pine green, oxblood red and inky black with thin gold borders, embossed crests, a crowned heraldic emblem and engraved copperplate capitals. Labels sit within delicate frames of double rules and tiny ornamental flourishes. Wax-seal accents, tissue paper, fine marbled endpaper patterns, tartan ribbons and glossy lacquered boxes with satin linings add collector charm. Lettering is spaced classical serif in gold on black or dark ink on cream. Eccentric, English, refined and gently theatrical.'),
('Laduree','Europe','1860s-present','confectionery','In the style of Laduree, dainty, sugary Second Empire Parisian elegance. Pastel colours in pistachio green, rose pink, lilac, vanilla yellow, powder blue and coffee brown are laid out in soft ombre blocks. Rigid pale mint or pink surfaces carry a gold embossed oval emblem ringed with a thin laurel-like wreath and a flowing gold script wordmark. Fine gilt edges, satin ribbon, tissue wrapping and delicate arabesque trellis and floral lattice patterns in cream and gold give a fine, porcelain-like finish. Small cherub and garland motifs, scalloped borders, matte velvety coatings and soft pearly sheen keep the mood feminine and polished. Sweet, precious, ladylike and gently nostalgic.'),
('Harrods','Europe','1900s-present','retail','In the style of Harrods, opulent, ceremonial British luxury in deep pine green and gold. Glossy lacquered or patent-like dark olive green surfaces carry a plain gold serif wordmark in a refined upright cut, often framed by a thin gold rectangular border and a small crest. Carrier-bag style flat panels, ribbon trim, gold foil stamping, tonal embossing and polished brass details give a rich, heavy feel. Palette is dark green, antique gold, cream and burgundy, with occasional cream and terracotta stone-like tones. Fine rope-like cord, tassels, silk lining and quilted textures add comfort. Layouts are symmetrical and centred with generous margins. Dignified, heritage-rich, gilded and grand.'),
('Selfridges','Europe','1900s-present','retail','In the style of Selfridges, bold, confident, high-impact British modernism built on one saturated sunshine yellow. Flat, even solid yellow surfaces carry a heavy black sans-serif capital wordmark in tightly packed lettering, sometimes cropped off the edge or blown up very large. Black twisted cord and plain black trim sit against the yellow with crisp contrast. Paper-like matte and semi-gloss finishes keep surfaces simple and graphic. Alternate colourways use hot pink, electric blue, lime and monochrome black and white in the same blunt layout, with a small ampersand-style mark. Little ornament, just strong blocks, large type and sharp edges. Loud, witty, fashionable and unmistakable.'),
('In-N-Out','North America','1950s-present','restaurant','In the style of In-N-Out, clean, retro Californian, bright and uncluttered. White fields carry red lettering in a chunky rounded italic outline, with a bright red and yellow boomerang-like arrow swoosh and a pair of crossed yellow palm-like shapes. Repeating borders of small red palm-tree motifs and slim red bands run along white paper and cardboard surfaces, with simple flat red and white colour blocking and glossy printed coatings. A limited palette of red, white and sunny yellow keeps everything crisp. A tiny thin red script phrase sits beneath the name. Matte uncoated paper and shiny red lacquered details. Fresh, nostalgic, honest and sunny.'),
('Nandos','Europe','1990s-present','restaurant','In the style of Nandos, warm, bold, casual, spicy and lively. A stylised black and red rooster emblem with a heart on its chest sits beside a heavy hand-cut wordmark in glossy chilli red or black. Palette runs through chilli red, terracotta, burnt orange, sunny yellow, teal, mint and soft peach, set in flat blocks. Surfaces carry African-inspired geometric patterns, bold arcs, semicircles, sun discs, zigzags and hand-printed abstract portraits with a screen-print look. Kraft cardboard and matte paper in warm earth tones are cut into angular tabs with colourful striped trims and rough linocut edges. Playful, cheeky short-hand lettering in black on bright fields. Vibrant, sociable, handmade and fiery.'),
('Pret a Manger','Europe','1990s-present','cafe','In the style of Pret a Manger, brisk, tidy, natural urban freshness. A deep burgundy-maroon star-shaped roundel carries the name in tall condensed uppercase letters within a thin ring of small lettering, set on white, kraft brown or cream. Surfaces are matte, with warm paper textures, clear glass and brushed steel accents. A secondary palette of leafy green, mustard, cobalt blue and berry pink appears in seasonal flat patterns of dots, leaves, snowflakes and confetti on bright wrapping. Stripes of burgundy on cream and small star sprinkles repeat as trim. Labels are plain, with thin rules and honest, friendly lowercase notes. Clean, healthy, quick and modern.'),
('Trader Joes','North America','1990s-present','retail','In the style of Trader Joes, friendly, quirky, nautical-tiki neighbourhood charm. A red hand-lettered script wordmark with a casual brush swing sits inside a round red ring emblem on natural cream canvas and kraft paper. Small tote-style forms in off-white canvas have contrasting navy, forest green, mint, yellow or sky-blue edge piping. Flat hand-drawn illustrations of vegetables, fruit, fish, sailing boats, flowers and cows in primary red, green, yellow and blue fill patchwork-like panels. Matte paper, cotton weave and chalk-like lettering give a homemade quality, with witty whimsical captions, small woodcut-style islands and tropical leaves. Cheerful, thrifty, wacky and welcoming.'),
('Qantas','Oceania','1970s-present','airline','In the style of Qantas, sunny, friendly, sporty and bold. A sweeping vivid red triangular wedge with a curved edge carries a white stylised leaping animal silhouette with a streamlined, stretched body. The wordmark is set in clean, wide, upright capitals in white on red or red on white, often italic and tightly spaced. Colour blocking uses bright white, strong poppy red, soft grey and a thin dark charcoal accent, with a smooth high-gloss painted finish and crisp edges. Warm outback tones such as terracotta, sand and ochre appear as a secondary accent, plus a pale sky blue. Simple, geometric and graphic, with confident curves. Optimistic, athletic, proud and clean.'),
]
